# FABLE-OPUS-P0-SIZEOF-ATOM-20260924-157: `c.sizeof(...)` is an ordinary c.* door call.  P0 no longer
# keeps it as one raw atom, so its non-c.* operand is an L2 expression like any door operand's: an
# own int x is lowered (`c.sizeof(l2_tN)`), where the raw atom left the name `x`, which C does not
# know.  The c.* token operand stays raw.  Success is 7.
fn: own_bytes () size_t
    int: x
    return: c.sizeof(x)
end: own_bytes

fn: check () int
    if: own_bytes() != c.sizeof(c.int)
        return: 81
    return: 7
end: check

sendMessage: exit(exit_code: check(); stdout: ""; stderr: "")
return
